- LazeCode's UI is inspired by PyCharm and implemented in its own code. The
  project does **not** ship JetBrains source code, icons, or other binary
  assets.
- PyCharm and JetBrains are trademarks of JetBrains s.r.o. The names are used
  only to describe design inspiration and compatibility, not as trademarks or
  to suggest affiliation. LazeCode is not affiliated with or endorsed by
  JetBrains.
- No telemetry is uploaded, and there is no account system or crash-reporting
  service. A small local-only diagnostics buffer can be enabled in Settings;
  it never leaves the machine. The only automatic network request is the
  optional update check (on by default, at most once a day, against this
  repository's GitHub Releases; it can be disabled in Settings). Git remotes
  and any language servers you configure may make their own network requests.
